This package vendors and adapts the "edu-chem-reaction" skill from the
edulab project.

Upstream source : https://github.com/wy51ai/edulab
Skill path      : skills/edu-chem-reaction
License         : Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE.upstream)
Author          : wy51ai (edulab)

Faithfully vendored (unmodified in behavior):
  - reaction_kernel.py       (lib/reaction_kernel.py) — sympy balancing,
                             conservation/mapping check, bond-diff, scene assembly
  - molecules.py             (lib/molecules.py) — VSEPR molecule geometry library
  - reaction_template.html   (template/reaction.html) — Three.js + KaTeX data-driven template

Added for backend integration (original work, same Apache-2.0 terms):
  - render.py    : render assembled data into the template, returning an HTML
                   string (no filesystem write, no cwd dependency).
  - presets.py   : the reaction build_* presets + REGISTRY (adapted from
                   scripts/generate.py) plus generate_reaction_html(key).
  - extract.py   : chemistry detection + classification of lesson content into a
                   supported reaction preset (or None).

RDKit is optional and is NEVER auto-installed; the VSEPR library is used when
RDKit is unavailable. The upstream Apache-2.0 license text is retained in
LICENSE.upstream.
